cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository or its artifacts, please cite it as below.
title: >-
  Beyond Perturbation Robustness: Do Genomic Foundation Models Learn
  Biological Equivalence?
abstract: >-
  Code, frozen sequence cohorts, embeddings, statistical results and figures
  for an evaluation of whether genomic foundation models represent
  synonymous (protein-preserving) coding-DNA edits differently from
  edit-matched nonsynonymous controls. Four models are evaluated on nested
  human CDS cohorts: Omni-DNA-20M, Omni-DNA-116M, NucEL-93M and
  JEPA-DNA-NTv3-100M.
type: software
